          "description": "Creates a Batch, without jobs, and answers with it: the \`agent\` every job added to it runs, set once, its labels and its failure breaker. Add its jobs with \`POST /batches/{id}/jobs\`. The hub checks the Output contract's schema, refusing one that is invalid, describes a list or refers outside itself. A \`customId\` makes the creation safe to retry: the same \`customId\` with the same \`agent\`, \`labels\` and \`breaker\` answers with the Batch already created, and with any of them different is refused.",
          "name": "create",
