          "description": "Resumes a stopped job and answers with the job. A paused, failed or cancelled job goes back to \`queued\` and carries on from where it stopped, on the Runner that holds its work; one paused before it started simply starts. Resuming a job that is queued or running changes nothing, and one that gives it other limits than its own is refused: its run keeps them. A job whose pause its Runner has not yet confirmed, whose cancel waits, that succeeded, that never started before it ended, or whose Batch is cancelled, is refused. A job resumed while its Batch is paused is \`queued\` and waits for the Batch. A resume that changes the job may give it a new \`runTimeoutSeconds\` and \`modelBudgetUsd\`, and is refused when the job's model calls have cost its \`modelBudgetUsd\` or more, as for a job that failed with \`modelBudgetExceeded\`.",
